---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
---

<Layout title="Teaching">
  <h1>Teaching &amp; Mentoring</h1>
  <p>
    I'm passionate about teaching, and about helping other people find and
    chase their own passions in STEM. Here's where I've gotten to do that,
    from Berkeley classrooms to the lab bench.
  </p>

  <div class="card">
    <h3>Biological Performance of Materials</h3>
    <p class="pub-meta">BIOE/MSE C118/C208 &middot; UC Berkeley &middot; Instructor: Dr. Kevin Healy</p>

    <p style="font-weight: 700; color: var(--pink-700); margin-bottom: 0.1rem;">
      Reader
    </p>
    <p class="pub-meta">Fall 2026</p>
    <p>
      I grade homework, exams, and team design projects for a class of 33
      students.
    </p>

    <p style="font-weight: 700; color: var(--pink-700); margin-top: 1.75rem; margin-bottom: 0.1rem; padding-top: 1.5rem; border-top: 1px solid var(--line);">
      Guest Lecturer
    </p>
    <p class="pub-meta">2023 &ndash; 2026</p>
    <p>
      I've taught four full lectures in place of the instructor, including two on
      hydrogels, one on polymers and viscoelasticity, and an introduction to
      polymers.
    </p>

    <p style="font-weight: 700; color: var(--pink-700); margin-top: 1.75rem; margin-bottom: 0.1rem; padding-top: 1.5rem; border-top: 1px solid var(--line);">
      Graduate Student Instructor
    </p>
    <p class="pub-meta">Fall 2022</p>
    <p>
      For a class of about 40 students, I led a weekly discussion section,
      held office hours, and graded homework and exams. I also evaluated
      about 10 team design projects, in which students proposed biomaterial
      solutions to unmet clinical needs through a pitch, two presentations,
      and a 15-page report.
    </p>
  </div>

  <div class="card">
    <h3>Clinical Need-Based Therapy Solutions</h3>
    <p class="pub-meta">BIOE 252 &middot; UC Berkeley &middot; Instructor: Dr. Syed Hossainy</p>
    <p style="font-weight: 700; color: var(--pink-700); margin-bottom: 0.1rem;">
      Reader
    </p>
    <p class="pub-meta">Fall 2026</p>
    <p>
      In a graduate course of about 100 students, I form and guide student
      teams developing therapy concepts for unmet clinical needs, grade
      homework and team projects, and coordinate guest lecturers from around
      the country.
    </p>
  </div>

  <div class="card">
    <h3>Mentoring in the Lab</h3>
    <p class="pub-meta">Kevin Healy Lab, UC Berkeley &middot; 2022 &ndash; 2026</p>
    <p>
      I mentored three PhD rotation students, a visiting international PhD
      student, an undergraduate researcher, and a team of four Master of
      Translational Medicine students, and trained dozens of other students on lab equipment
      and methods along the way.
    </p>
  </div>

  <div class="card">
    <h3>Resident Assistant</h3>
    <p class="pub-meta">Northeastern University &middot; August 2017 &ndash; July 2019</p>
    <p>
      As a live-in mentor for about 45 first-year women each year pursuing careers
      in STEM, I helped residents set goals, connect with
      scientists and professors, and access resources for their academic
      and scientific goals. I also designed
      programs like Q&amp;A panels with graduate students and faculty,
      leadership workshops, and mentorship events.
    </p>
  </div>

  <div class="card">
    <h3>Advancement Via Individual Determination (AVID)</h3>
    <p class="pub-meta">Volunteer Tutor &middot; Fenway High School &middot; September 2018 &ndash; December 2018</p>
    <p>
      At Fenway High School in Boston, I led a weekly group of 6 to 8
      students in AVID, a program that prepares students from
      underrepresented and low-income backgrounds for college. Rather than
      handing out answers, I taught students to help each other work through
      challenging math and science problems by asking good questions and
      thinking critically. Hearing students worry about whether a school
      like Northeastern, just a five-minute walk away, was within reach
      made me want to break down those barriers to STEM.
    </p>
    <a
      class="btn secondary"
      href="https://www.avid.org/"
      target="_blank"
      rel="noopener noreferrer"
    >
      Visit AVID
    </a>
  </div>

  <div class="home-cta">
    <a class="btn" href="/community/">See My Community Work</a>
  </div>
</Layout>
